      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T10:52:26Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(edm): sinker side burn - a lateral electrode move that burns one wall out by a stated amount\n\nA separate op kind, Sinker Side Burn (stored id 42): the Sinker Burn's\nplunge with its own condition, then one Feed along +X/-X/+Y/-Y at the\nfloor and back. Its own electrode undersize with the condition's spark\ngap bounds the move: allowance = undersize - gap; a move past it (a move\ninto the part), a gap the undersize can't honour, an unknown condition,\na non-finite/zero/negative amount and an orbit are refused by name at\ncommand creation (create, paste, edit, retype) and again at generation.\nThe box atom sweeps every move; MCP through the params JSON door;\nadditive file variant. CL golden sinker_side_burn.cl.\n\nNot exercised on a real EDM control.\n\nFixes #545\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
